// The launcher's default keybindings, as VS Code ships its own.
//
// The entry chord, the pickers' chords, and cmd+k for a row's actions, which
// every launcher has. Moving and opening inside a picker --
// quickOpen.selectNext, quickOpen.accept, quickOpen.back, quickOpen.hide --
// is yours to bind: arrows, return and escape work without a binding. Yours
// go in ~/.config/commandlayer/keybindings.json, added after these; a
// command starting with "-" removes earlier entries for it -- only that key
// when it names one.
//
// "global": true binds a key in every app, while the layer is closed too;
// the rest work only while it is open. alt+space is Raycast's and Alfred's
// default too: whichever of them holds it has to give it up.
//
// A picker with a prefix is a mode of the root, so its chord opens the root
// with that prefix typed.
[
  { "key": "alt+space", "command": "quickOpen", "global": true },
  { "key": "cmd+k", "command": "quickOpen.showActions" },
  { "key": "cmd+o", "command": "quickOpen", "args": { "view": "palette" } },
  { "key": "cmd+r", "command": "quickOpen", "args": { "view": "recent" } },
  { "key": "cmd+.", "command": "quickOpen", "args": { "view": "context" } },
  { "key": "cmd+p", "command": "quickOpen", "args": { "view": "files" } }
]
